Unicorn is a development-only comparison backend, excluded from production
packages. Its GPL-2.0 and included dependency notices remain in the development
installation. The pinned 2.1.4 source is available at
https://github.com/kxrxh/doodle-jump-mgu/releases/download/v0.2.1/unicorn-2.1.4.tar.gz
(SHA-256: 00567a70e323f749b419cd86bee4f9115beab7ebba32194581c090cbb7c59cff).
The local unicorn-write-protect.patch (2026-11-16) refreshes cached translations
after a handled write-protection callback. The patch and tools/prepare_unicorn.py
build recipe are retained in the source repository.
The C++ components statically link GCC libstdc++ and libgcc (GPL-3.0-or-later
with GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1); their notices and license are in
the runtime licenses directory.

Shop, toy purchases, restore-purchase entry points, ad-removal buttons and promotions are
omitted from drawing and input. This does not grant paid entitlements. Advertising,
payment, account and online platform SDKs are not loaded by this offline host.
News is omitted from rendering and input as well. The package excludes unused
store and game-over promotional assets and unused _X PNG variants, retaining the
host's _X font atlas and the original _L images for every theme. Included gameplay
textures retain their original bytes, and all game sounds are retained.

Peripheral scenery uses crops of the original gametiles_L.png and live bck_ paper;
crop coordinates and paper projection are recorded in runtime/host/src/images.rs
and runtime/host/src/drawing.rs. Wrapped source texels and the renderer's public
linear filter preserve the repeating paper edges. The added app icon and cursor
are separate new assets. Shipping PNG files retain their creation prompts in metadata.

MGU toolkit: https://github.com/cauliflowermossgrape/idrive7-apps
Revision: cca7f9ad17f96b92e60a89ea98686afe1b662041
See kit/LICENSE. The WebAssembly renderer uses the GPL-3.0-or-later and original
MIT notices in native/doodle-gpu/LICENSE and native/doodle-gpu/LICENSE.mgu-renderd.

The separately installed doodle-gpu worker presents game textures through EGL
and a Wayland surface attached to the game's existing compositor layer. The
Wayland IVI protocols are COVESA wayland-ivi-extension 1.11.0 (MIT, DENSO
CORPORATION and BMW Car IT GmbH); their original notices are retained in the
protocol XML and LICENSE.ivi. The worker also provides an I420 VIDEO path for
systems where native surface presentation is unavailable.
Its scene executor originated in the Doodle Jump GPU extension to mgu-store
revision cc39c1470fd25c4c39605dbe2965139f7d97ce1d:
https://github.com/robertnisipeanu/mgu-store
The worker is GPL-3.0-or-later and retains the original renderer's MIT notice
as LICENSE.mgu-renderd. Complete sources and the build recipe ship as
doodle-gpu-source-2.1.1.tar.gz and are in native/doodle-gpu.

App source builds download and verify the original APK and game assets. Ready app
packages include those files. The source repository excludes the original files;
the runtime release includes the translated game module, while the app build adds
the original ARM library and assets.
